 DevOps Interview Command Series — Grafana (Day 14) 📈

Grafana is the visualization layer of observability.
It helps DevOps & SRE teams turn metrics into actionable insights using dashboards, alerts, and data sources like Prometheus, Loki, CloudWatch, and more.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Grafana commands & operations you must know:

grafana-server -v

systemctl start grafana-server
systemctl status grafana-server
systemctl restart grafana-server

grafana-cli plugins list-remote
grafana-cli plugins install plugin-name
grafana-cli plugins update-all

curl http://localhost:3000/api/health
curl -u admin:password http://localhost:3000/api/datasources
curl -u admin:password http://localhost:3000/api/search

# Common Grafana Query Usage (Prometheus)
rate(http_requests_total[5m])
sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total[5m])) by (pod)
node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes
histogram_quantile(0.95, rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m]))

